{"status":"completed","summary":"node1 now has a persistent firewalld policy that allows SSH and TCP/8080 and explicitly rejects unrelated inbound connections. Restart persistence and post-restart behavior were verified. No application was installed on port 8080; the firewall permits it for a future service.","actions_performed":["Preserved RHEL 10.0 and kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64.","Configured the public zone with target REJECT, SSH service allowed, and TCP/8080 allowed.","Removed unrelated Cockpit and DHCPv6-client inbound exceptions.","Verified behavior through an isolated ingress path using live listeners: TCP/22 and TCP/8080 accepted; TCP/8081 rejected.","Restarted node1 safely and proved its boot identity changed.","Verified firewalld, sshd, persistent policy, and direct ingress behavior after restart.","Removed all temporary test listeners, network namespaces, interfaces, and logs."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Persistent firewall permits SSH and TCP/8080 while rejecting unrelated inbound connections","command_ids":["cmd-804cd1892eea443a","cmd-d350f9bd9be14d36","cmd-97510a18f9004605"],"summary":"Runtime and permanent zones show explicit REJECT with only SSH and TCP/8080 allowed. Direct pre- and post-restart tests accepted ports 22 and 8080 while rejecting a live service on 8081."},{"requirement":"Installed OS release and kernel remain unchanged","command_ids":["cmd-70c8ee5a7ac64031","cmd-a58e3586e10d44bd"],"summary":"Both baseline and post-restart evidence show RHEL 10.0 and kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64."},{"requirement":"node1 mandatory restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-6b54340664d643cb","cmd-ff02a8a303c34053","cmd-f04ecbdceb8e4e65","cmd-a58e3586e10d44bd","cmd-97510a18f9004605"],"summary":"Baseline boot ID was 21972395-6444-42bf-8e37-5c3108194a7d; the safe reboot was acknowledged; recovered boot ID was 8384da27-f5e6-4b28-a1ff-1dbdb951a84d. firewalld and sshd recovered active/enabled, persistent policy was restored, and direct allow/reject behavior passed after restart."}]}
